1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535156 true] [17592186334340 1111 #uuid "f8a47ab9-58a1-5e66-98c1-7ec2dc3ab4ee" 13194139535156 true] [17592186334341 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334342 13194139535156 true] [17592186334341 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334348 13194139535156 true] [17592186334341 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334353 13194139535156 true] [17592186334341 1089 "q-337395" 13194139535156 true] [17592186334341 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535156 true] [17592186334341 1100 "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y=2x-5.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." 13194139535156 true] [17592186334341 1113 #uuid "bc82baf7-6e13-5137-9b62-5ced3f36541b" 13194139535156 true] [17592186334341 1145 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{x})}^{′}-(u{e}^{x}) & =2x-5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x}-u{e}^{x} & =2x-5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{x}+\\cancel{u{e}^{x}}-\\cancel{u{e}^{x}} & =2x-5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{x} & =2x-5 \\\\ {u}^{′} & ={e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & ={e}^{-x}(2x-5) \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535156 true] [17592186334342 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334343 13194139535156 true] [17592186334342 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334344 13194139535156 true] [17592186334342 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334345 13194139535156 true] [17592186334342 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334346 13194139535156 true] [17592186334342 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334347 13194139535156 true] [17592186334342 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535156 true] [17592186334342 1041 "field-1" 13194139535156 true] [17592186334342 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334346 13194139535156 true] [17592186334342 1110 #uuid "f3c6b39e-c0e6-5e97-b21d-45795ae718eb" 13194139535156 true] [17592186334343 1034 "u(x){e}^{-2x}" 13194139535156 true] [17592186334343 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535156 true] [17592186334343 1111 #uuid "45b747e4-2547-559c-94e6-c31c4087f78e" 13194139535156 true] [17592186334344 1034 "u(x){e}^{5x}" 13194139535156 true] [17592186334344 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535156 true] [17592186334344 1111 #uuid "9675e90c-04c4-575a-bb2c-e0e709f70828" 13194139535156 true] [17592186334345 1034 "u(x){e}^{2x}" 13194139535156 true] [17592186334345 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535156 true] [17592186334345 1111 #uuid "49ca8f81-e15c-50ed-a80f-2153a5ffdd94" 13194139535156 true] [17592186334346 1034 "u(x){e}^{x}" 13